# RAG Quality Standard

## Pipeline Architecture

```
intent_classifier → [off_topic → off_topic_responder → END]
                 → metadata_extractor
                 → query_translator
                 → retriever (hybrid dense+sparse, RRF)
                 → relevance_grader
                 → generator
                 → groundedness_grader
```

### Components
| Component | File | Responsibility | Model |
|---|---|---|---|
| intent_classifier | `ml/nodes/intent_classifier.py` | Classify query into 7 intents | **3B** (needs reliable reasoning) |
| off_topic_responder | `ml/nodes/off_topic_responder.py` | Immediate refusal, bypasses RAG | — |
| metadata_extractor | `ml/nodes/metadata_extractor.py` | Extract hard filters + `exclude_skills` | **3B** (guardrail-critical extraction; 1B hallucinated hard filters) |
| query_translator | `ml/nodes/query_translator.py` | Rewrite into 3 diversified search queries | **1B** (template generation) |
| retriever | `ml/nodes/retriever.py` | Hybrid Qdrant search (dense+sparse) + RRF | — |
| relevance_grader | `ml/nodes/relevance_grader.py` | Filter results + apply `exclude_skills` | **3B** (grades up to 20 docs) |
| generator | `ml/nodes/generator.py` | Intent-specific prompt → LLM answer | **3B** (quality matters) |
| groundedness_grader | `ml/nodes/groundedness_grader.py` | Hallucination detection | **3B** (needs accuracy) |

### LLM Provider & Split-Model Strategy

The provider is **auto-selected** at startup via `ml/llm_service.py` (`AbstractLLMService` DIP pattern):
- **`GROQ_API_KEY` set** → `GroqLLMService` (cloud, LPU-accelerated — recommended)
- **No key** → `OllamaLLMService` (local fallback)

| Mode | Heavy model | Light model | Latency |
|---|---|---|---|
| Groq (cloud) | `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` | `llama-3.1-8b-instant` | ~1–3 s |
| Ollama (local CPU) | `llama3.2` (3B) | `llama3.2:1b` (1B) | ~60–120 s |

**Split-model rationale:** `query_translator` uses the light model because it does template-like query diversification. `metadata_extractor` intentionally uses the heavy model even though it returns structured JSON: hallucinated hard filters silently empty Qdrant results, so correctness matters more than latency. Heavy nodes (`intent_classifier`, `metadata_extractor`, `relevance_grader`, `generator`, `groundedness_grader`) require reliable reasoning or guardrail accuracy and get the larger model.

**Config keys:** `GROQ_API_KEY`, `GROQ_LLM_MODEL`, `GROQ_LIGHT_LLM_MODEL` in `.env`.

### Intents
| Intent | Trigger | Special behavior |
|---|---|---|
| `find_matching` | Default — find vacancies | — |
| `role_transition` | "switch roles", "move to X" | Excludes current role from results |
| `compare` | "which is better", "best from these" | Returns single winner with justification |
| `clarify_vacancy` | Follow-up on specific vacancy | Targets previously mentioned vacancy |
| `followup` | Refining previous query | Uses chat history to apply delta filters |
| `aggregate` | Synthesis across many vacancies | Widens `top_k` to 20, broad retrieval |
| `off_topic` | Non-job-related query | Early exit — canned refusal response |

