## Metrics & Observability

### Real-time Metrics (collected on every query)
Every completed pipeline run writes one row to the `query_stats` PostgreSQL table.

| Field | Type | What it measures |
|---|---|---|
| `total_latency_ms` | int | End-to-end response time |
| `node_timings_ms` | JSON | Per-node wall-clock time (all 7 nodes) |
| `intent` | str | Classified user intent |
| `retrieved_count` | int | Vacancies returned by retriever |
| `graded_count` | int | Vacancies that passed relevance grading |
| `is_grounded` | bool | Groundedness grader result |
| `was_fallback` | bool | No answer generated (fallback text sent) |
| `was_off_topic` | bool | Query classified as off_topic |
| `retry_count` | int | Groundedness retry count |
| `input_tokens` | int? | Prompt token count (from Ollama response metadata) |
| `output_tokens` | int? | Completion token count (from Ollama response metadata) |

**Implementation:**
- `ml/timing.py` — `@timed_node("name")` decorator wraps every async node, stores `elapsed_ms` into `state["node_timings"]`
- `ml/nodes/generator.py` — reads `response.response_metadata["prompt_eval_count"]` / `eval_count`
- `chat/service.py` — after `rag_graph.astream()` finishes, assembles `QueryStat` from final state and calls `stats_repo.save()`
- `stats/repository.py` — aggregation functions (totals, averages, distributions)

**API endpoints:**
```
GET /api/v1/stats/         → aggregated summary
GET /api/v1/stats/recent   → last N query rows
```

### Stats Dashboard
URL: **http://localhost:5173/stats**

Displays: total queries · avg latency · fallback rate · off-topic rate · token counts · intent distribution bar chart · per-node latency bar chart · recent queries table with intent badge.

### Metric Categories

**Generation quality (offline Ragas eval):**
| Metric | Minimum | What it checks |
|---|---|---|
| Faithfulness | ≥ 0.70 | No hallucinations — answer only uses retrieved data |
| Answer Relevancy | ≥ 0.65 | Answer addresses the question asked |

**Retrieval quality (offline Ragas eval):**
| Metric | Minimum | What it checks |
|---|---|---|
| LLM Context Recall | ≥ 0.60 | Retriever surfaces the needed documents |
| LLM Context Precision | ≥ 0.60 | No noisy/irrelevant documents retrieved |

**Performance (real-time, `query_stats` table):**
| Metric | Source | What it measures |
|---|---|---|
| Latency (total + per-node) | `node_timings_ms` | Where time is spent in the pipeline |
| Token count | `input_tokens` / `output_tokens` | CPU load and generation cost |
| Intent Accuracy | `intent` field | Distribution of classified intents over time |
| Fallback Rate | `was_fallback` | How often the pipeline fails to produce an answer |
| Off-topic Rate | `was_off_topic` | How often users send unrelated queries |

